# Collaboration wrap

During the task, follow `.cursor/rules/elite-task-efficiency.mdc` (pick the
cheaper path first). Then when we finish a **project** or the user confirms a
**successful multi-step task** (good / done / lock this in / wrap validation /
what did we learn), run `@collaboration-wrap`:

1. Recap in chat (what finished, 1–3 learnings, next-time change).
2. **Wrap validation:** one short preference question when the next default
   needs their call. Skip only if already clear. After they answer, lock it in.
   Do not silently automate big habits without wrap validation.
3. Run the **efficiency pass**: one concrete way the next run is faster or
   simpler. Implement it if small and safe; otherwise write it into the owning
   Skill or rule.
4. Write durable behavior into the owning `.cursor/rules/` or Skill.
5. Do not add a new status or learnings Markdown file.

Skip wrap on tiny one-file edits. If the task was clearly successful and
multi-step, do the wrap without waiting to be asked.
